  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifesaving WASH intervention in Rural Damascus and Dar&apos;a governorates</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to improve safe and dignified access to adequate water and sanitation services for approximately 78,300 direct beneficiaries, contributing to Strategic Priority One of the SHF SA1 2024 Allocation Strategy.  Under Output 1.1, Oxfam aims to improve water access for 76,000 people through borehole, pumping station and water tank rehabilitation, network upgrades, and provision of Operation and Maintenance (O&amp;M) materials reducing costs of Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) services for House Holds (HH) and ensuring they have dignified access to water. Under Output 1.2., rehabilitating sewage network connections for 2,300 individuals to prevent water contamination, environmental damage, and hygiene and health risks caused by sewage network failures.</narrative>
  </description>
